</mrow></math><div class="formula-string">,</div></div><h5 class="label">(2)</h5></div>where
               <div class="def-list"><a class="usa-link" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7"><!-- named anchor --></a><div class="def-list table"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;margin-bottom: 2em;"><dl><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7aa"><p><i>P</i><sub>MMI7</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7ab2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7ab2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the probability of MMI 7 or greater ground motion,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b1a"><p><i>M</i><sub>main</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b1b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b1b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the mainshock magnitude,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b2a"><p><i>t</i><sub>0</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b2b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b2b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the candidate wait time,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b3a"><p><i>t</i><sub>e</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b3b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b3b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the planned duration of time inside a damaged building, and</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b4a"><p><i>N</i><sub>MMI7</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b4b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b7b4b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the expected number of instances of MMI 7 or greater ground motion.</p></dd></dl></div></div>
</div>
<div class="section"><a class="usa-link" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9"><!-- named anchor --></a><h3 class="series-title">Expected Number of Aftershocks</h3>
<p id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b3">The expected number of aftershocks of a given magnitude is calculated using the model
                     by <a class="usa-link" href="#ofr20261029-r22">Reasenberg and Jones (1989)</a>. We compute the number of aftershocks in magnitude bins with a step size of Δ<i>M</i>, which requires a factor of <span class="inline-formula"><math id="ofr20261029-m4" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:ali="http://www.niso.org/schemas/ali/1.0/" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
<mrow>
<mfenced>
<mrow>
<mn>1</mn>
<mo>−</mo>
<msup>
<mrow>
<mn>10</mn>
</mrow>
<mrow>
<mo>−</mo>
<mi>b</mi>
<mi>Δ</mi>
<mi>M</mi>
</mrow>
</msup>
</mrow>
</mfenced>
</mrow></math></span> to translate the cumulative number of events to the number within a bin. We model
                     aftershocks of magnitude 5 through <i>M</i><sub>main</sub>. The largest bin also contains all aftershocks larger than the mainshock, as the
                     MMI 7 footprint of these aftershocks all cover the entire MMI 7 footprint of the mainshock.
                     No maximum magnitude needs to be estimated because the details of the magnitude distribution
                     above <i>M</i><sub>main</sub> are not used. The expected number of aftershocks of magnitude <i>M</i><sub>aft</sub> ±0.5Δ<i>M</i> (or all events larger than <i>M</i><sub>aft</sub> −0.5Δ<i>M</i> for <i>M</i><sub>aft</sub>=<i>M</i><sub>main</sub>) is:
                     </p><div class="disp-formula panel"><a class="usa-link" id="ofr20261029-e03"><!-- named anchor --></a><div class="formula-content"><math display="block" id="ofr20261029-m5" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:ali="http://www.niso.org/schemas/ali/1.0/" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
