</mrow></math><div class="formula-string">,</div></div><h5 class="label">(3)</h5></div>where
                  <div class="def-list"><a class="usa-link" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5"><!-- named anchor --></a><div class="def-list table"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;margin-bottom: 2em;"><dl><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5aa"><p><i>N</i><sub>aft</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5ab2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5ab2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the expected number of aftershocks,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b1a"><p><i>M</i><sub>aft</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b1b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b1b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the aftershock magnitude,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b2a"><p><i>t</i><sub>0</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b2b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b2b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the candidate wait time,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b3a"><p><i>t</i><sub>e</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b3b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b3b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the planned duration of time inside a damaged building,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b4a"><p><i>a</i></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b4b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b4b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the aftershock productivity,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b5a"><p><i>b</i></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b5b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b5b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the earthquake b-value,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b6a"><p><i>M</i><sub>main</sub></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b6b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b6b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the mainshock magnitude,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b7a"><p>Δ<i>M</i></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b7b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b7b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the magnitude discretization,</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b8a"><p><i>c</i></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b8b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b8b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the aftershock time parameter, and</p></dd><dt class="def-term cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b9a"><p><i>p</i></p></dt><dd class="def-def cell" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b9b2"><p class="" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b5b9b2b1" style="margin-block-end: -1em;">is the aftershock decay parameter.</p></dd></dl></div></div>
</div>
<p id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b7">The values of the aftershock parameters (<i>a</i>, <i>c</i>, and <i>p</i>) for active continental, stable continental, and subduction zone interface earthquakes
                     are taken from <a class="usa-link" href="#ofr20261029-r19">Page and others (2016)</a>, using their ANSR-SHALCON, SCR-GENERIC, and SZ-GENERIC parameter values, respectively.
                     We also adopt the corresponding uncertainty in the <i>a</i>-value, which represents the aftershock productivity, to model the uncertainty in
                     the forecast. For subduction zone intraslab earthquakes, we use the parameter values
                     found by <a class="usa-link" href="#ofr20261029-r17">Michael and others (2020)</a> for the 2018 <i>M</i><sub>W</sub>7.1 Anchorage, Alaska, earthquake, and assign uncertainty corresponding to the largest
                     uncertainties reported by <a class="usa-link" href="#ofr20261029-r19">Page and others (2016)</a>. The assumed <i>b</i>-value for all cases is 1.0±0.05.</p>
<p id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b9">Alternatively, the expected number of aftershocks for a specific ongoing aftershock
                     sequence is available from the USGS aftershock forecast. These forecasts appear on
                     the mainshock “event page,” which can be found either through the USGS latest earthquake
                     map (<a class="usa-link" href="https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/map/" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b9b1" target="xrefwindow">https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/map/</a>) or through the USGS aftershock forecast information page (<a class="usa-link" href="https://earthquake.usgs.gov/data/oaf/" id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9b9b3" target="xrefwindow">https://earthquake.usgs.gov/data/oaf/</a>).</p>
<p id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b3b9c11">We developed a relation between aftershock probability and the probability of strong
                     shaking, so that users can reference the aftershock forecast to estimate risk. A simple
                     relation between the aftershock forecast and the probability of MMI 7 or greater shaking
                     is possible only for building entry durations equal to the duration of the forecast,
                     otherwise the solution also depends on the wait time <span class="inline-formula"><math id="ofr20261029-m6" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:ali="http://www.niso.org/schemas/ali/1.0/" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
<mrow>
<msub>
<mi>t</mi>
<mn>0</mn>
</msub>
</mrow></math></span>. We use a duration of 1 day, as this is available in the public USGS forecast. We
                     can rewrite <a class="usa-link" href="#ofr20261029-e03">equation 3</a> in terms of <i>P</i><sub>forecast</sub>, which is the probability of a magnitude <i>M</i><sub>forecast</sub> or larger earthquake within the next day:
                     </p><div class="disp-formula panel"><a class="usa-link" id="ofr20261029-e04"><!-- named anchor --></a><div class="formula-content"><math id="ofr20261029-m7" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:ali="http://www.niso.org/schemas/ali/1.0/" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
<mrow>
<msub>
<mi>N</mi>
<mrow>
<mi>a</mi>
<mi>f</mi>
<mi>t</mi>
</mrow>
</msub>
<mfenced>
<mrow>
<msub>
<mi>M</mi>
<mrow>
<mtext>aft</mtext>
</mrow>
</msub>
<mo>,</mo>
<msub>
<mi>P</mi>
<mrow>
<mtext>forecast</mtext>
</mrow>
</msub>
</mrow>
</mfenced>
<mo>=</mo>
<mfenced close="" open="{">
