<caption style="display: none;">Table 1.    Wait time (rounded to the nearest day) until probability of Modified Mercalli Intensity
                        (MMI) 7 or greater shaking from aftershocks is at or below 0.4 percent during the
                        entry period, for crustal mainshocks.</caption></table></div>
</div>
<p id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b5b7">The median and 84th percentile wait times until the probability of MMI 7 or greater
                  shaking at a single location reaches the threshold of 0.4 percent are shown in <a class="usa-link" href="#ofr20261029-t02">table 2</a> for subduction zone mainshocks. Note that the considered mainshock magnitudes for
                  subduction zones are larger than the considered mainshock magnitudes for continental
                  earthquakes. The wait times increase for larger magnitude mainshocks, similar to the
                  continental earthquakes. Wait times for subduction interface events are longer than
                  the wait times for subduction intraslab events, although the aftershock productivities
                  are similar. The intraslab events tend to be deeper, with fewer aftershocks producing
                  MMI 7 shaking at the earth’s surface.</p>
<div class="table-wrap panel" style="display: float; clear: both"><a class="usa-link" id="ofr20261029-t02"><!-- named anchor --></a>
<div><h3 style="display:inline;font-size: 1em;">Table 2.    </h3>Wait time (rounded to the nearest day) until probability of Modified Mercalli Intensity
                        (MMI) 7 or greater shaking from aftershocks is at or below 0.4 percent during the
                        entry period, for subduction zone mainshocks.</div><sup class="caption" style="font-size: 85%;top: 0.5em;">
