</div>
<p id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b5c15">The median and 84th percentile aftershock probabilities <i>P</i><sub>forecast</sub> corresponding to a 0.4 percent probability of MMI 7 or greater shaking at a single
                  location are shown in <a class="usa-link" href="#ofr20261029-t04">table 4</a> for subduction mainshocks. For subduction mainshocks, we use the forecast for a reference
                  magnitude of <i>M</i><sub>forecast</sub>=6, because the considered mainshock magnitudes are larger than the considered mainshock
                  magnitudes for continental earthquakes and the probabilities of <i>M</i>5 aftershocks start saturating near 100 percent. Instead of waiting a prescribed time,
                  as in <a class="usa-link" href="#ofr20261029-t02">table 2</a>, a user can wait until the forecast probability is at or below the level in <a class="usa-link" href="#ofr20261029-t04">table 4</a>. Again, the threshold probabilities <i>P</i><sub>forecast</sub> increase for larger magnitude mainshocks.</p>
<div class="table-wrap panel" style="display: float; clear: both"><a class="usa-link" id="ofr20261029-t04"><!-- named anchor --></a>
<div><h3 style="display:inline;font-size: 1em;">Table 4.    </h3>Threshold probability of a magnitude [<i>M</i>]≥6 aftershock within the next day, for subduction zone mainshocks. Waiting until
                        the forecast probability is at or below this threshold achieves a 0.4 percent or lower
                        probability of Modified Mercalli Intensity (MMI) 7 or greater shaking from aftershocks
                        during the next day.</div><sup class="caption" style="font-size: 85%;top: 0.5em;">
<h4 aria-hidden="true" class="subsection-title"></h4>
<p id="ofr20261029-w56ab1b7b1b1b5c17b1b3" style="display:inline;">[%, percent]</p>

</sup>
